          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "নেভা (nebhā) is the plain partner of নেভানো, \"to put out\", from Sanskrit nirvāyati, \"is extinguished\" (CDIAL 7399)."
